{"name":"Applause Please","hex":"#858c9b","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"applause","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The act of applauding; approbation and praise publicly expressed by the clapping of hands, stamping or tapping of the feet, acclamation, huzzas, or other means; marked commendation."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To applaud."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/applause"},{"term":"please","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To make happy or satisfy; to give pleasure to.","To desire; to will; to be pleased by."]},{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["Used to make a polite request."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/please"}],"entries":[{"title":"Applause","blocks":[{"text":"Applause is primarily a form of ovation or praise expressed by the act of clapping, or striking the palms of the hands together. Audiences usually applaud after a performance, such as a concert, speech or play, as a sign of enjoyment, approval, and praise."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/Arabic_arts_festival_applause.jpg/330px-Arabic_arts_festival_applause.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Applause","wikidata":"Q814696"},{"title":"Please","blocks":[{"text":"Please is a word used in the English language to indicate politeness and respect while making a request. Derived from shortening the phrase \"if you please\" or \"if it please(s) you\", the term has taken on substantial nuance based on its intonation and the relationship between the persons between whom it is used. In much of the Western world, use of the word is considered proper etiquette, and parents and authority figures often imprint upon children the importance of saying \"please\" when asking for something from an early age, leading to the description of the term as \"the magic word\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6e/Southdown_bus_199_%28KUF_199F%29%2C_2009_Amberley_Bus_Day.jpg/330px-Southdown_bus_199_%28KUF_199F%29%2C_2009_Amberley_Bus_Day.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Please","wikidata":"Q26175857"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/Aleksey_Semenenko%2C_Kyiv_Syphony_Orchestra%2C_Kurhaus_Wiesbaden.jpg/500px-Aleksey_Semenenko%2C_Kyiv_Syphony_Orchestra%2C_Kurhaus_Wiesbaden.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/Aleksey_Semenenko%2C_Kyiv_Syphony_Orchestra%2C_Kurhaus_Wiesbaden.jpg/1280px-Aleksey_Semenenko%2C_Kyiv_Syphony_Orchestra%2C_Kurhaus_Wiesbaden.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/Aleksey_Semenenko%2C_Kyiv_Syphony_Orchestra%2C_Kurhaus_Wiesbaden.jpg/500px-Aleksey_Semenenko%2C_Kyiv_Syphony_Orchestra%2C_Kurhaus_Wiesbaden.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The violinist Aleksey Semenenko comes to receive applause after performing in concert with the Kyiv Symphony Orchestra at the Kurhaus, Wiesbaden, conducted by Luigi Gaggero, who stands at the back of the stage.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAleksey_Semenenko%2C_Kyiv_Syphony_Orchestra%2C_Kurhaus_Wiesbaden.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8c/Visual_Applause_for_the_Deaf.jpg/500px-Visual_Applause_for_the_Deaf.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8c/Visual_Applause_for_the_Deaf.jpg/1280px-Visual_Applause_for_the_Deaf.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8c/Visual_Applause_for_the_Deaf.jpg/500px-Visual_